### Why 6.13.4 and not newer

Checked 2026-11-17 via https://registry.npmjs.org/ethers/latest:
the latest ethers 6.x is **6.17.0** (published 2026-06-17).
Decision: **stay on 6.13.4, do not update.** Reasons:

- 6.13.4 is the version verified working end to end, including one
  real live mint (Pocket Moons, 2026-11-11, trigger-to-receipt 2.0s).
- The 6.14.0–6.17.0 changelog entries are feature/provider work
  (request-rate throttle, ENSv2/cointype fixes, EIP-7594 blob-proof
  helpers, non-canonical-S signature handling, Etherscan provider
  fixes). None of them is a security fix for the surface this skill
  uses (ABI encoding/decoding, `parseEther`/`formatEther`,
  `keccak256`/`id`, `Interface`, `getAddress`).
- Replacing the vendored 505 KB bundle without a live mint to
  re-verify it would trade a verified artifact for an unverified one.
  Revisit the update only together with a live dry-run + live mint
  re-verification, and record the new SHA-256 here when that happens.

